</section>

<section class="section wrap" id="work">
  <div class="sechead">
    <h2>Systems that ship, teams that deliver, and customers that buy</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="intro">My work sits where architecture meets the people who have to live with it, and engineers get better at their craft along the way.</p>
  {% set quote = "Organizations exist in as much as they provide service to humans." %}
  {% set from = "what-in-the-world-is-world-class-engineering-part-2" %}
  {% set fromTitle = "What in the World Is World-Class Engineering? Part 2" %}
  {% include "epigraph.njk" %}
  <div class="cards">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 1</p>
      <h3>Stack Overflow</h3>
      <p class="muted">Director of Product Engineering, Acting Principal Architect</p>
      <p>Led two full-stack teams maintaining the Public Platform and led the Architecture Group. We doubled deploy frequency, cut build times by 20%, and delivered a six-month redesign on microservices and microfrontends on schedule. I also helped develop the company's AI productivity program, including an MCP server and AI hackathons.</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>deploy frequency</dt><dd>2×</dd></div>
        <div><dt>build times</dt><dd>−20%</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 2</p>
      <h3>Pluralsight</h3>
      <p class="muted">Senior Director, Acting Principal Architect</p>
      <p>Oversaw architecture for an engineering org of 300 to 500 people across 65+ teams in the US, India and Australia. Connected product structures to architecture and payment systems, built identity and audit systems, and worked closely with Security.</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>teams</dt><dd>65+</dd></div>
        <div><dt>continents</dt><dd>3</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 3</p>
      <h3>Merrick Bank</h3>
      <p class="muted">Acting Principal Architect</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>engineers</dt><dd>2 → 16</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>Helped grow engineering from 2 people to 16 and wrote the hiring process. Led payment processing work and built identity, authorization and audit trail systems.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n &lt; 3</p>
      <h3>Earlier</h3>
      <p>Equis International/Reuters, ProTel Networks, HRN and Galileo, including global teams, technical pre-sales, and point-of-sale and payment systems.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

